body:
@ncw Sorry for taking so long to answer. I've lost some of the files after doing ``rclone dedupe`` (because they were in "My Computer" zone added to "My Drive", so files deleted in one place are also deleted in the other). It was my fault for no having a backup for all of them and also because the remote was not read only, but it would be great if, by default, you make ``dedupe`` not delete duplicates, just list them and ask for confirmation. 

I suppose though that the fact that there were duplicates (which in reality weren't duplicates, just links between "My Drive" and "My Computers") shouldn't matter the size, though, as the remote I'm running ``size`` against is the root of "My Drive", so "My Computers" shouldn't be handled by rclone at all.

I'm still restoring/finding the backup of some of my files, so will leave this on hold for a while until I figure some things out. Whenever I can I will post you the results of the other commands you requested.
